Subject: [PATCH 02/29] fix(scalar-uint-xor): re-freeze bitEffects'
 whole_program_sha256 for corpus 0ed489ec

The 0ed489ec corpus bump changed classicNoisedeck/bitEffects/bitEffects.glsl
by exactly one comment line (the noisemaker source-URL rename from
noisedeck/noisemaker@master to noisefactorllc/noisemaker@main). Whoever
carried the corpus bump through this profile updated raw_sha256/
raw_bytes/normalized_sha256/normalized_bytes/functions_sha256 correctly
(all of those already matched the new corpus), but missed
whole_program_sha256 -- the one fingerprint that hashes program.raw_source
verbatim (byte-for-byte, comment included) rather than the
comment-stripped normalized source or derived structures.

Verified directly: re-parsed the new corpus source through the same
analyze_program(parse_program(...)) pipeline the test/profile use, and
every other field in the frozen record (raw/normalized bytes+sha,
functions_sha256, interface_sha256, function_inventory_sha256,
bindings_sha256, resources, loop) already matched -- only
whole_program_sha256 was stale. Recomputed it from the live analyzed
program and pinned the new value.

This was the sole cause of 5 errors + 2 failures in test_scalar_uint_xor.py
(test_all_seven_exact_carriers_authenticate_three_owned_lanes,
test_authentication_returns_objects_from_each_supplied_tree,
test_biteffects_signed_and_vector_xors_are_not_authorized,
test_each_carrier_rejects_missing_duplicate_reordered_and_retyped_sites,
test_exact_uint_to_float_census_selects_only_grain_observable_site,
test_the_other_six_keys_keep_the_stricter_absent_set); all 19 tests in the
module now pass (Ran 19 tests ... OK).

Note: _PROFILES["synth/noise:noise"] has the same latent staleness (same
whole_program_sha256 drift) but is never exercised by the current suite --
_load_program() always routes synth/noise:noise through
apply_runtime_loop_bound first, which converts it to a dynamic program
before authenticate_scalar_uint_xor ever consults _PROFILES for that key.
Left alone: no test exercises it, and I don't have proof of the entry's
correct exercised shape to re-freeze it responsibly. Flagging for whoever
next touches noise's runtime-define profile.

